# Pull requests (standard)

When the user asks to create a pull request, use `gh` and follow this format. Do not open a PR unless asked.

## Before opening

1. Ensure the branch is pushed (`git push -u origin HEAD` if needed).
2. Base branch: `main` unless the user specifies otherwise.
3. Title uses **Conventional Commits** (same types/scopes as commit messages):  
   `feat(bot): …`, `fix(parser): …`, `docs: …`

## Body template (required)

Pass the body via HEREDOC:

```bash
gh pr create --base main --title "<conventional title>" --body "$(cat <<'EOF'
## Summary
- <1–3 bullets: what changed and why>

## Test plan
- [ ] <concrete verification step>
- [ ] <another step if needed>

EOF
)"
```

## Rules

- Summary focuses on **why** / user impact, not a file dump.
- Test plan is a checklist the reviewer can actually run (unit tests, curl, smoke, manual WA check when relevant).
- Do not include secrets, `.env` values, or tokens in the PR body.
- Return the PR URL when done.
- Do not push or open a PR unless the user explicitly asked.

## Example

**Title:** `feat(bot): add internal DM endpoints and issue reminder transport`

**Body:**
```markdown
## Summary
- Expose `/internal/send-text-dm` and `/internal/send-document-dm` for Core/saasDelivery
- Add idempotent issue reminder sending via the health server

## Test plan
- [ ] `npx jest src/__tests__/unit/botOutboundTextDm.test.js`
- [ ] `npx jest src/__tests__/unit/botHealthServer.test.js`
- [ ] On bot VPS after deploy: curl dry-run `POST /internal/send-text-dm` with valid token
```
